# Build context for every image build: both workflows use `context: .`, so this
# file is the only place non-build inputs can be trimmed before the checkout is
# uploaded to the builder and captured in the type=gha build cache.
#
# The Dockerfile reads exactly six context paths: go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, api/,
# and internal/ in the builder stage, and dist/ in the binaries-prebuilt stage.
# Everything below is excluded because no stage reads it.
#
# dist/ is deliberately absent: `BINARIES=prebuilt` copies it, so CI builds
# depend on it reaching the builder. hack/ is excluded for the same reason it is
# never copied -- the coordinator-go runtime check bind-mounts the workspace and
# runs hack/ from there, it is not baked into the image.

# Version control and CI definitions.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local build and test output.
bin/
cover.out

# Prose, the docs site, and the Helm chart.
*.md
docs/
site/
charts/

# Developer-only sources and kubebuilder scaffolding.
hack/
config/

# Release packaging output and dependency-automation metadata.
.release/
.release-please-manifest.json
release-please-config.json
renovate.json
